# PART 2: MEMBER PORTAL — REDESIGN THE VISUAL EXPERIENCE

This is one of the most important modifications.

I want the MEMBER PORTAL to adopt the same dashboard-style visual architecture as the EXECUTIVE DASHBOARD.

The two interfaces should share a consistent design language, navigation philosophy, sidebar structure and page layout.

However, their functions and permissions must remain different.

## 2.1 Main design principle: Vertical information hierarchy

The current member interface needs improvement because information and feature options arranged excessively horizontally are easily overlooked.

Think of how people read newspapers and articles.

People naturally scan and scroll through vertically arranged information.

I want the member experience to use this principle.

Avoid:

- Excessively wide horizontal feature arrangements.
- Important options hidden in horizontal scrolling rows.
- Horizontal carousels for primary navigation.
- Tiny cards arranged in long horizontal strips.
- Interfaces that require users to discover essential functions by scrolling sideways.

Prioritise:

- Vertical information flow.
- Clearly labelled sections.
- Full-width content blocks.
- Vertically stacked information cards.
- Readable announcements.
- Generous spacing.
- Easily discoverable navigation.
- A clear content hierarchy.

On desktop, the member portal should have a persistent left sidebar and a main content area.

On mobile, the sidebar should collapse into a hamburger menu.

